// What the registry currently contains, as data the API can check against.
//
// Everything between the markers is generated by scripts/build-site.py from
// data/entries.json and data/vocab.json. Do not edit it by hand: `python3
// scripts/build.py` rewrites it, and CI rebuilds and fails on any difference.
//
// Why generate it rather than read the JSON at runtime. A Vercel function that opens
// data/entries.json depends on that file being traced into the bundle, which is a
// deployment detail that fails quietly and only in production. A generated module is
// imported like any other, is visible in review as a diff, and cannot disagree with the
// vocabulary the build enforces, because the same run writes both.
//
// This is the same device build-site.py already uses for app.js, which cannot read
// data/vocab.json in a browser either. One source, two generated copies, both checked.

